    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Christian Yelich** (70.50) and **Yordan Alvarez** (69.65) headlining our offensive attack. **Christian Yelich** is our premier play, benefiting from a favorable matchup against Zebby Matthews; his score is buoyed by a dynamic platoon advantage and a high-probability stolen base environment thanks to the pitcher's slow delivery. **Yordan Alvarez** remains a must-start despite the platoon disadvantage against Robbie Ray, as his elite xwOBA of 0.473 provides a high floor that renders standard matchup concerns secondary. **Kyle Schwarber** (66.09) and **Trea Turner** (64.41) also present strong value, with **Trea Turner** specifically providing the necessary speed profile to attack the stolen base category, though both carry exposure to a 33% rain risk in their respective matchups against Jos\u00e9 Soriano.\n\nRegarding our bench decisions, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (54.25) was the most difficult exclusion, narrowly missing the cut behind **Nelson Velazquez** (55.77). While **Pete Crow-Armstrong** benefits from an elite leadoff spot, the optimizer ultimately pivoted to **Nelson Velazquez** due to a more favorable matchup against Ryan Feltner, whose high xERA (4.85) offers a higher ceiling for counting stats. We are also monitoring the status of **Kazuma Okamoto** (45.11), who draws a difficult assignment against Zack Wheeler. While his raw projection is suppressed by Wheeler\u2019s elite 2.85 xERA, his spot in the batting order and inherent park factors keep him in the lineup, provided he clears the 33% rain risk. We will continue to track the final lineups for **Dillon Dingler**, **Gary Sanchez**, **Caleb Durbin**, **Colt Keith**, **Junior Caminero**, **Carson Benge**, **Lars Nootbaar**, **Josh Smith**, **Chase Meidroth**, **Jacob Gonzalez**, **Hector Rodriguez**, **Luis Pena**, and **Pedro Ramirez** to ensure our daily efficiency remains optimal as we navigate the unavailability of **Casey Schmitt**.",
